  "question": {
    "text": "Let $f(x)$ be continuous on $[0,5]$ and differentiable in $(0,5)$. If $f(0)=0$ and $\\left|f^{\\prime}(x)\\right| \\leq \\frac{1}{5}$ for all $x$ in $(0,5)$, then $\\forall x$ in $[0,5]$.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ExiII",
      "text": "$|f(x)| \\leq 1$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "y5m3a",
      "text": "$|f(x)| \\leq \\frac{1}{5}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DSiPn",
      "text": "$f(x)=\\frac{x}{5}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "lW8rX",
      "text": "$|f(x)| \\geq 1$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\left|f^{\\prime}(x)\\right| \\leq \\frac{1}{5}, \\Rightarrow\\left|\\frac{f(x)-f(0)}{x-0}\\right| \\leq \\frac{1}{5}$\n$\\Rightarrow\\left|\\frac{f(x)}{x}\\right| \\leq \\frac{1}{5}, \\quad|f(x)| \\leq \\frac{|x|}{5} \\Rightarrow|f(x)| \\leq 1 \\quad\\left(0 \\leq x \\leq 5 \\Rightarrow 0 \\leq \\frac{x}{5} \\leq 1\\right)$",
    "image": null
  },
